    h('Online/offline; hybrid edge/cloud; batch/streaming')
    p('Offline jobs generate data, fit chemical preprocessing/OOF predictions, train transaction models, calibrate thresholds and validate versioned bundles. Online scoring reads the event and current customer state, derives features before updating state, joins chemical consistency and returns score/review reasons. A laboratory workstation can cache chemical probabilities by sample and measurement/model version; a central service maintains cross-device customer history and the review queue. Connectivity and privacy favour keeping raw laboratory records local; central event history enables velocity detection. This is a proposed hybrid architecture, not a deployed cloud service.')
    p('Sequential customer events use batch 1 with per-customer ordering preserved. Cross-customer microbatches up to 32 can improve throughput without mixing history states. Batch reconciliation is offline. Review processing is asynchronous, and cached chemical outputs are invalidated after record or model changes. Event IDs support idempotency. Late/out-of-order events require replay or manual review, never silent history mutation. The local demo implements state and input checks; shared storage, queues and API hosting are future components.')
